'''Ancient Egg: N205''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[June Bride of the Devil (Event Gacha)|June Bride of the Devil]] event. It was added in [[Version 13.4 Update|Version 13.4]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 757
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N205
|name2 = Violet Egg: N205
|name3 = Bride Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Violet Egg: N205''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bride Cat''' at level 30.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, reverting to this form may prove useful if a cheaper, more spammable meatshield is needed in an [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] stage.

==='''True Form'''===
A surprisingly decent event egg unit, Bride Cat is effective at being an early-game [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]], [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]], and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu Cat]], and a decent anti-Zombie melee unit to boot. With its somewhat low cooldown and decent stats against target traits, it is serviceable to deal with Aku and Zombie enemies early on, especially against Behemoths like [[THE FOLIVOREAN]], [[Vermilingua Rangmaster]], and [[Formicidaean Ariant]]. It is exceptional at dealing with many zombies, as it has enough range to outrange a majority of them, though it may be a bit inconsistent versus [[Zang Roo]] due to only outranging her by 5. Do take note of their ridiculously long recharge time (for a meatshield) of 6.5 seconds though, which is even longer than [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu Cat]]'s recharge times! Because of this, they absolutely need help from Combos such as [[Bad Guys (Combo)|Bad Guys]] or [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]]. Overall though, they are a decent unit if you have the stones to afford it and lack the aforementioned options, as it is outclassed by their superior stats. But at least for those who unlock it rather early in the playthrough, this cat will secure a happy wedding.

